00:42:54.370 --> 00:42:57.670
for a triangle you do the base times the

00:42:57.670 --> 00:43:01.420
height times one-half for the volume of

00:43:01.420 --> 00:43:02.500
a pyramid

00:43:02.500 --> 00:43:04.450
you do one-third the area of the base

00:43:04.450 --> 00:43:06.160
whatever shape this is you find the area

00:43:06.160 --> 00:43:08.440
if it's a square or triangle or hexagon

00:43:08.440 --> 00:43:12.250
times the height okay for a cylinder the

00:43:12.250 --> 00:43:14.320
volume equals the area of the base PI R

00:43:14.320 --> 00:43:17.080
squared times the height the surface

00:43:17.080 --> 00:43:18.790
area equals two PI R squared that's the

00:43:18.790 --> 00:43:21.520
two circles plus two pi RH that's the

00:43:21.520 --> 00:43:24.130
lateral area or the sides in a cone the

00:43:24.130 --> 00:43:27.340
volume equals 1/3 PI R squared times the

00:43:27.340 --> 00:43:30.070
height and I'll just maybe mention one

00:43:30.070 --> 00:43:32.380
quick example that comes up on the AC T

00:43:32.380 --> 00:43:34.300
and that's it sometimes they'll ask you

